A||||6||dogtired||FIRE Just my Luck!||||8||
Z||000000||dogtired||07-09-2000||07:06 AM||||If it weren't for bad luck I wouldn't have any luck at all!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>Well I didn't think my 86GT was old enough to smoke, but tonight, well this AM my daughter (yes the Fuzzy dice) called. She was in my GT, sure couldn't have been her SE. She said she was just crusin about 60MPH when the car acted like it just died? Pushed down on the gas and nothing then the check engine light came on (will be interesting to see if it set a code), while pulling over to the side of the road she saw flames and smoke comming out of the battery grill  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> You want to talk about PANIC!<P>Well it wasn't that major, when I have my back back and I can rebuild everything, so far at this point I haven't gotten to see much cause it is still dark out. Not even sure if it was electrical or something elce, oil for fuel, thinking if it were fuel the whole car would have been deep fried? It did flame up on the front side of the motor, (just testing the FIRE wall?) cooked lots of wiring, melted cables and now there is a small pool of what looks like oil under it?? Fried the deck a small amount. So will check it out, looks like the need for parts has arrived??<BR>What a wonderful Weekend  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000001||Wolfhound||07-09-2000||08:11 AM||||Sorry to hear about the fire. Glad to hear the damage is minor and your daugter it OK.<BR>Battery side? Oil pressure sending unit??<BR>Coy ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||07-09-2000||10:42 AM||||Dog--Glad to hear your daughter is fine.  Too bad about the car, though.  If there are any parts I might have (mostly Iron Duke stuff, but you never know) feel free to email me and ask for them.  I'll do what I can to help out.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||07-09-2000||11:27 AM||||Good thing you have a parts car or two.||||reg||1
