Z||000005||dogtired||07-09-2000||06:08 PM||||Thanks for all the Support Gang!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I haven't tore into it yet to perhaps discover the cause. Since I have fire, theft and glass breakage coverage, I will let the insurance Co. look at it on Monday and see what they will do. Then its my turn.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Seems like I just talked about fires here on the Forum a day or two ago?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> Back in the mid late 60's when driving 57 chevrolets, I carried fire extinguishers, had one of them melt down because of a backfire through the carb.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Guess its time to put an extinguisher in each Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Ill keep ya all informed as to WHY THIS Happened? Maybe I can help you save Yours?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000006||Gokart||07-10-2000||06:45 AM||||Thanks dog and good luck. Glad to hear your daughter is OK. How did the fire go out? Did it run out of things to burn? I hope you find the damage minimal and be careful of your back when you start ripping things apart!<P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||2
